{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\nWhitespace-only changes to a ticket description invalidate its signed plan-review attestation, forcing an unnecessary (slow, costly) re-review before the close gate will accept the ticket.\n\n## Repro (observed this session on 28cd-d8f8-4456-482c)\n1. A ticket has a certified/signed plan review at description length 7098 chars (ending in a single trailing newline).\n2. Re-set the description via `rebar edit --description=\"$(cat file)\"` — shell command substitution strips the trailing newline, so the stored description becomes 7097 chars. The visible content is byte-identical apart from that one trailing \\n.\n3. `rebar review-plan <id> --status` returns `{\"ok\": false, \"verdict\": \"stale-material\", \"reason\": \"the plan was materially edited since review — changed: description (7098 -> 7097 chars)\"}`.\n4. `rebar transition <id> in_progress closed` is blocked by the plan-review close gate with 'stale-material' and demands a fresh `review-plan`.\n\nNote (contrast): ticking acceptance-criteria checkboxes (`- [ ]` -> `- [x]`) is correctly hash-invisible and does NOT invalidate the review. Only the insignificant-whitespace delta (a trailing newline) drifted the material fingerprint.\n\n## Expected\nPlan-review material canonicalization should normalize insignificant whitespace before hashing so that whitespace-only edits — trailing/leading newline differences, trailing spaces on a line, and analogous no-semantic-change edits — do not invalidate a signed plan review or trip the stale-material close gate. Only semantically meaningful description changes should drift the material.\n\n## Impact\nAn operator ticking ACs and re-saving a description (a routine close-time step, and one where CLI $(...) newline-stripping is easy to hit) can be forced into a full LLM re-review (~7-15 min + model spend) purely for a trailing-newline difference. This wastes gate budget and slows the close path, and risks tempting a --force bypass.\n\n## Suggested fix direction\nIn the plan-review material builder (the description material-part hash, currently reported like 'description <hash> <char-count>'), apply a canonicalization pass (e.g. strip trailing whitespace per line + normalize trailing newlines to a single canonical form, consistent with how AC-checkbox state is already normalized out) before fingerprinting. Add a regression test asserting that a trailing-newline-only edit keeps review-plan --status 'certified'.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Adding or removing a trailing newline (or trailing whitespace on lines) in a ticket description does not change the plan-review material fingerprint, so a previously signed review stays 'certified' per `rebar review-plan <id> --status`.\n- [x] The plan-review close gate does not report 'stale-material' for a whitespace-only description edit.\n- [x] A regression test drives: sign a review, apply a trailing-newline-only description edit, assert `review-plan --status` stays certified and the close gate is not blocked on stale-material.\n- [x] Semantically meaningful description edits still correctly invalidate the review (the normalization does not over-collapse real changes)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786112244333893001,"uuid":"6b198922-5854-4650-8d3a-2513807afde1"}